I said all session that exp6968 needed a post-fix eval run, including when
proposing the run and when it was authorized. Wrong. Its artifact shows five
of six preconditions passing since 03:52Z, including having found a
content-matched engine. The one failure is immutable_transition_source, which
the experiment evaluates as 'source is not None'. I never opened the artifact.

The run emitted four engines regardless, and each new evidence directory
carries transitions.jsonl and envelope.json beside the engine, which the old
flat files never did. Recorded as a hypothesis that this addresses the real
blocker, not as a result: nobody has run exp6968 against them.

Separately and concretely: all four landed in the evidence-directory shape and
none as a flat wm_*.py. arc_induction_quality.py globs world_model.py and
attempts/wm_*.py and never descends into attempts/evidence/, so the engines
are invisible to the scorer built to grade them. The producer contract shipped
today without moving its consumer. Filed as an operator decision rather than
widened here, because the alternative is to have the producer emit both shapes
and that is a contract choice.

